# HS3 (docs/ui-fit/README.md, "2j"). Every phone surface that draws an error or
# status line in its layout, with exactly how many. `pnpm check:stays-put`
# fails on any file missing here, and on any count that no longer matches, in
# either direction.
#
# One entry per line: `<sites> <path>`. A blank line ends a group, and each
# group's `#` lines must include one starting `Content:` (the line is the
# screen's own content, not news of a tap) or `Grandfathered:`. A new entry,
# or a raised count, goes in its own group under `Content:`; it never joins or
# raises the grandfathered group. The way out is `<Notice>` (@some-ui/shared),
# which says it on the plane over the screen and is not a site.
#
# This file is where HS3 is reviewed. The check counts; it does not judge.

# Grandfathered: these drew lines in their layout before HS3 landed. Debt,
# not a judgment that each is fine: a count here may only fall (lower it in
# the same change), and an entry leaves when its file says it with Notice.
